ity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State that the self-heal marker re-materialization in the list path is atomic/idempotent under concurrent lists (e.g. write_marker's fcntl handling makes it safe, or it takes the appropriate lock), so the check-then-act cannot race.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5a","T5b","T5e","T7","T9"],"criteria":["T9"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'when a reduced ticket's compiled state says archived but the .archived marker file is absent, re-materialize it via reducer.marker.write_marker'","'the registry runs all units under the store write lock' — but the list path is a read path with no lock stated","ABSENCE: no statement of concurrency/idempotency for the self-heal write under concurrent list calls"],"finding":"The reader self-heal writes a marker file (write_marker) during the list/read path when a marker is absent — a check-then-act (marker absent -> write) that two concurrent list calls could both perform; the plan does not state whether this write is serialized/atomic or whether the list path holds a lock, unlike the ensure unit which explicitly runs under the store write lock.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f8b6e383544a29525","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / Scope: src/rebar/reducer/_api.py self-heal re-materialize","norm_id":"nd6437682a0bf2f2e","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Two `list` invocations race on the same net-archived ticket with a missing marker and both call write_marker","A list runs concurrently with an archive/compaction that is mutating markers"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Add one line to the Approach: note that write_marker is idempotent and atomic (fcntl-guarded), so concurrent list calls converge on the same marker without corruption; confirm the list path need not hold the store write lock for this.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Note the sequencing/back-out: the self-heal reader change must ship in the same (or an earlier) release than the untrack unit, and state the back-out (re-add markers via write_marker / revert the untrack commit) so the fast-path degradation window is explicit.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5a","T5b","T5e","T7","T9"],"criteria":["T4"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.7,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'that is safe for correctness because listing excludes archived tickets from compiled state, and the marker is only a fast-path'","ABSENCE: no explicit ordering that the self-heal reader ships before the untrack unit runs, and no back-out note for the untrack commit"],"finding":"When the untrack commit merges into a peer whose deployed reader does NOT yet contain the self-heal code, that peer's `.